      "description": "Watch Rennes vs Marseille highlights and goals from Ligue 1 on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 11, 2026. On September 11, 2026 , Ligue 1 fans were treated to a high-octane encounter as Rennes hosted Paris Saint Germain . The match was a tale of two halves, characterized by clinical finishing and a relentless tactical battle that saw the momentum swing dramatically under the stadium lights. Rennes Take Command Early Rennes started the match with incredible intensity, catching the visitors off guard with their rapid transitions. The breakthrough came just 9 minutes in when Sebastian Szymanski unleashed a stunning left-footed strike from outside the box into the top corner, following a neat setup by Adrien Thomasson . Paris Saint Germain struggled to find their rhythm, and despite efforts from João Neves , they found themselves further behind in the 38th minute. A precise cross from Przemyslaw Frankowski found Estéban Lepaul in the center of the box, who made no mistake with a right-footed finish to double the lead. Rennes went into the break with a commanding 2-0 advantage, while the visitors were left searching for answers after Brice Samba pulled off several key saves to deny Ousmane Dembélé and company. The Ferran Torres Recovery The second half saw a total transformation from Paris Saint Germain following the introduction of Ferran Torres . The substitute became the focal point of the attack, and in the 71st minute, he brought his side back into the game. After a VAR review confirmed the goal, Torres finished clinically from the center of the box assisted by Fabián Ruiz . The pressure from the capital club became suffocating as they chased the equalizer. That equalizer arrived in the 82nd minute when Fabián Ruiz turned provider once again, delivering a cross that Ferran Torres headed into the bottom right corner. The final moments were frantic; Ludovic Blas nearly snatched a winner for Rennes , while Mika Godts missed a golden opportunity for PSG in stoppage time. The match ended 2-2, a result that highlighted the resilience of the champions and the ambition of the hosts."
