      "description": "Watch Angers vs Rennes highlights and goals from Ligue 1 on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 6, 2026. On September 6, 2026, Angers and Rennes faced off in a highly anticipated Ligue 1 encounter where every tactical move felt like a high-stakes chess match. Both sets of fans expected a battle of nerves, and the players delivered a spectacle filled with momentum shifts and late controversy. Early Dominance from the Visitors The match kicked off with high intensity, but it was Rennes who found their rhythm first. Just nine minutes into the contest, the deadlock was broken. Przemyslaw Frankowski showed clinical precision, finding the back of the net with his left foot after a well-timed assist from Sebastian Szymanski . The early goal stunned the home crowd and gave the visitors a platform to dictate the pace of the game, which was further solidified in the 17th minute when an unfortunate own goal by Jordan Lefort doubled the advantage for Rennes . The Angers Response Things looked bleak for the hosts, but Angers refused to crumble. As the first half progressed, they began to pile on the pressure, largely through the delivery of Branco van den Boomen . Their persistence paid off in the 35th minute when Carlens Arcus rose highest to head home a corner from Van den Boomen , cutting the deficit and reigniting the atmosphere inside the stadium. The goal shifted the momentum, turning what seemed like a one-sided affair into a competitive scrap heading into the interval. Late Drama and VAR Controversy The second half saw both managers turn to their benches to influence the flow, with Angers introducing fresh legs like Boulaye Dia and Usman Simbakoli . The closing stages were nothing short of breathless. In the 89th minute, Simbakoli came agonizingly close to a leveler, but his header crashed off the crossbar . As the game entered stoppage time, chaos ensued. Angers appealed frantically for a penalty, prompting a lengthy VAR check . After reviewing the footage at the monitor, the referee upheld his initial decision not to award the spot-kick, allowing Rennes to escape with a narrow victory despite the intense late pressure from the home side."
